+-- names, item names, Pokédex entries -- is already French when a French ROM
+-- is imported: it is decoded from the player's own cart at import time and
+-- never lives in this repository (see src/core/RomText.lua, which prefers the
+-- extracted line and only falls back to the literal below).
+--
+-- What this file covers is the text Gen1Recomp *authors*: menu labels, option
+-- rows, PC/box/bag prompts this port added, printer and save messages.  Those
+-- were English literals in Lua, which is what made a French import read half
+-- French and half English.
+--
+-- Keys are the exact English sources, the same convention a translation mod
+-- uses (src/core/Strings.lua).  An entry that is missing falls through to
+-- English, and Strings.get still checks format arity, so a wrong %s count
+-- here is reported and the English source is used instead of crashing.
